  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Minburn Technology Group obligated $767M in FY2026 to date across 437 awards, with an average award size of $1.8M. Minburn Technology Group obligations were down 19.0% year over year. Minburn Technology Group received its largest FY2026 to date obligations from the General Services Administration at $263M, the Department of Veterans Affairs at $142M, and the Department of State at $140M. Minburn Technology Group markets are concentrated in software and IT services, led by Other Computer Related Services at $394M and Software Publishers at $353M. Fiscal-year obligations for Minburn Technology Group show prior-year peaks in FY25 at $946M and FY24 at $927M, while earlier years include FY23 at $796M, FY22 at $494M, and FY21 at $559M. All figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. Current-year totals for Minburn Technology Group are partial, reflecting fiscal year to date reporting.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which federal agencies buy most from Minburn Technology Group?",
        "body": "General Services Administration is the top buyer of Minburn Technology Group with $263M in obligations. Department of Veterans Affairs follows with $142M, and Department of State follows with $140M. Department of the Treasury and Department of Energy round out the top five with $78.1M and $55.6M respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive Minburn Technology Group revenue?",
        "body": "Other Computer Related Services is the largest market for Minburn Technology Group at $394M. Software Publishers is the next largest at $353M. Smaller markets for Minburn Technology Group include Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $11.1M and Computer Terminal and Other Computer Peripheral Equipment Manufacturing at $7.9M."
      }
    ]
